From: yinjiayi <yinjiayi@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Include cstdint for public fixed-width integer types

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Upstream: https://github.com/jonathonl/shrinkwrap/tree/eaac292b255b5de45d6546a794ffbd103335bc40
Upstream-Status: Not submitted; standard C++ header dependency portability.

The three compression headers use std::uint8_t and other fixed-width integer
types but rely on transitive includes to declare them. GCC on openEuler fails
when compiling the unchanged original test program. Include the defining
standard header directly in each affected public header. No algorithm, feature,
test, assertion, compression backend or compiler option changes.
Remove when the official source directly includes cstdint in these headers.

--- a/include/shrinkwrap/gz.hpp
+++ b/include/shrinkwrap/gz.hpp
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #ifndef SHRINKWRAP_GZ_HPP
 #define SHRINKWRAP_GZ_HPP

+#include <cstdint>
 #include <streambuf>
 #include <array>
 #include <vector>
--- a/include/shrinkwrap/xz.hpp
+++ b/include/shrinkwrap/xz.hpp
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #ifndef SHRINKWRAP_XZ_HPP
 #define SHRINKWRAP_XZ_HPP

+#include <cstdint>
 #include <streambuf>
 #include <array>
 #include <vector>
--- a/include/shrinkwrap/zstd.hpp
+++ b/include/shrinkwrap/zstd.hpp
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@

 #include <zstd.h>

+#include <cstdint>
 #include <streambuf>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <vector>
